---
import Brand from "../../components/Brand.astro";
import Link from "../../components/Link.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Satstream — Bitcoin's data layer | Alejandro Martínez"
  description="Solo engineer behind Satstream: a multi-protocol Bitcoin indexer indexing the full chain into a 4-database cluster, with 5 SDKs and an MCP server."
>
  <div class="page"> 

    <!-- top bar -->
    <header class="topbar">
      <Brand />
      <nav class="topbar-nav">
        <Link href="/">← back</Link>
        <Link href="/#case-studies">case studies</Link>
        <Link href="mailto:alex@konar.es">contact</Link>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <!-- hero -->
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-tag">CASE STUDY · 02</div>
        <div class="hero-main">
          <div class="hero-meta">BITCOIN DATA INFRASTRUCTURE &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2024 — NOW &nbsp;·&nbsp; SOLE ENGINEER</div>
          <h1 class="hero-h1">I built Bitcoin's data layer.</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            Satstream is a multi-protocol Bitcoin indexer and API. One engineer, nine repositories,
            five SDKs, an MCP server and a block explorer. It indexes the full Bitcoin chain — UTXOs,
            inscriptions, BRC-20 ops, Runes etchings, Ordinals charms — into a multi-database cluster
            for sub-second queries.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-links">
          <div class="hero-links-label">LINKS</div>
          <Link href="https://satstream.io" class="hero-link">satstream.io ↗</Link>
          <Link href="https://github.com/satstream" class="hero-link">github.com/satstream ↗</Link>
          <Link href="https://docs.satstream.io" class="hero-link">docs · openapi spec ↗</Link>
          <Link href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/ss-mcp" class="hero-link">mcp server (npm) ↗</Link>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- numbers strip -->
    <div class="numbers">
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">REPOS</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">9</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">github.com/satstream</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">COMMITS</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">~350</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">sole consistent committer</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">CHAIN INDEXED</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">~3 TB</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">utxos · inscriptions</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">SDK LANGUAGES</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">5</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">go · js · python · rust · ts</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell">
        <div class="numbers-key">DATABASES</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">4</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">mongo · scylla · pg · redis</div>
      </div>
      <div class="numbers-cell numbers-cell--last">
        <div class="numbers-key">PROTOCOLS</div>
        <div class="numbers-val">3</div>
        <div class="numbers-sub">brc-20 · runes · ord.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- the brief -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="THE BRIEF" title="Make Bitcoin queryable like a database.">
      <p class="body-para">
        Bitcoin's RPC is fine for nodes and miserable for applications. Anyone shipping a wallet,
        explorer or DeFi product against BRC-20, Runes or Ordinals ends up writing the same indexer
        twice — once badly, once again with the lessons. Satstream is that indexer, written once,
        operated as infrastructure, exposed as a clean REST API and as an MCP server for AI agents.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- architecture -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="ARCHITECTURE" title="Nine repos, four datastores, one API surface.">
      <pre class="arch-diagram">  ┌─ bitcoin node (full archival, ~3 tb)
  │
  ├──▶ ss-indexer            [ go · mongo · grpc ]   core blocks · runic / non-runic split
  │      └──▶ runestone-decoding  [ grpc microservice ]
  │
  ├──▶ satstream-brc20-indexer    [ rust · mongo ]   brc-20 ops + runes etchings/mints
  │
  ├──▶ satstream-delta-indexer    [ rust · scylladb ]   per-address sat deltas
  │      (migrated from mongo for write throughput)
  │
  └──▶ charms-extractor           [ python · cassandra ]   ordinals charm attributes
                                              │
                                              ▼
                              ┌─ ss-api  [ go · fiber ] ──┐
                              │   14 endpoint categories  │
                              │   mongo · scylla · redis  │
                              │   stripe metering         │
                              └────────────┬──────────────┘
                                           │
       ┌───────────┬───────────┬───────────┼────────────┬────────────┐
       ▼           ▼           ▼           ▼            ▼            ▼
   sdk · go    sdk · js    sdk · py    sdk · rust    sdk · ts    ss-mcp (bun)
       (5 sdks generated from one openapi spec)               llm-native surface
</pre>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- decisions -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="DECISIONS" title="Five calls that earned their complexity.">
      <div class="decisions-grid">
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">01 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Migrate deltas to ScyllaDB</div>
          <p class="decision-body">MongoDB couldn't keep up with per-address UTXO write throughput. ScyllaDB's wide-column model and tunable consistency fits append-heavy, high-cardinality writes; the migration happened before the bottleneck became a production incident.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">02 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">gRPC microservice for Runestone decoding</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Pulled Runes protocol parsing into its own gRPC service consumed by the Go indexer. Clean protocol boundary; ScyllaDB writers don't ship with a Bitcoin script interpreter compiled in.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">03 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">OpenAPI as the canonical spec</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Five SDKs (Go, JS, Python, Rust, TypeScript) generated from one OpenAPI spec. Type-safe clients across every ecosystem developers actually use. Zero drift between languages.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">04 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">MCP server for AI agent access</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Shipped ss-mcp alongside the SDKs. The full API surface is natively callable by Claude, Cursor and every MCP-aware agent — no custom integration required. New onramp, same backend.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">05 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">Adaptive concurrency in the indexer</div>
          <p class="decision-body">adaptative_concurrency.go tunes worker pools at runtime instead of hard-coding thread counts. Indexer throughput tracks node IO instead of getting wedged at the configured ceiling.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision reveal-item">
          <div class="decision-tag">06 &nbsp;·&nbsp; DECISION</div>
          <div class="decision-title">HA Ord server config</div>
          <p class="decision-body">Primary + backup Ord servers configured directly in ss-api (OrdMainServer, OrdBackupServers) — inscription queries survive ord-server restarts without an external load balancer.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- ownership -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="OWNERSHIP" title="The nine repositories I shipped.">
      <div class="ownership-scroll"><div class="ownership">
        <div class="ownership-header">
          <span>REPO</span>
          <span>STACK</span>
          <span class="text-right">OWNED / TOTAL</span>
          <span class="text-right">ROLE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">ss-api</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">go · fiber · mongo · scylla · redis · stripe</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">127 / 132</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">owner</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">satstream-brc20-indexer</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">rust · mongo</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">107 / 107</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">ss-core</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">go · postgres · stripe</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">31 / 31</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">satstream-delta-indexer</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">rust · scylladb · prometheus</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">29 / 29</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">ss-indexer</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">go · mongo · grpc</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">21 / 23</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">owner</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">satstream-delta-indexer-go</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">go · cassandra</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">19 / 19</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">charms-extractor</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">python · cassandra · prometheus</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">13 / 13</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">ss-mcp</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">typescript · bun</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">—</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">sole</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ownership-row">
          <span class="ownership-repo">hex-cdk-infra</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim">go · aws cdk · ecs · alb</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">—</span>
          <span class="ownership-dim text-right">owner</span>
        </div>
      </div></div>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- outcome -->
    <div class="reveal-section">
    <section class="section" data-section-tag="OUTCOME" title="Bitcoin infrastructure, built solo.">
      <p class="body-para">
        Satstream required simultaneous depth in Bitcoin protocol internals (UTXO model, BRC-20 spec,
        Runestone format, inscription model) and production distributed systems engineering
        (ScyllaDB write throughput, gRPC service boundaries, Prometheus instrumentation, AWS CDK).
        Nine repositories, sole committer on seven of them. The MCP server extends the data layer
        to AI agents — the same Bitcoin data that was previously only queryable via REST is now
        natively callable by any MCP client.
      </p>
    </section>
    </div>

    <!-- next case -->
    <div class="next-case">
      <span class="next-case-label">NEXT CASE STUDY</span>
      <Link href="/cases/crossflow" class="next-case-link">
        03 &nbsp; Crossflow Network — TSS/MPC cross-chain protocol →
      </Link>
    </div>

    <!-- footer -->
    <footer class="footer">
      <span>alejandro martinez · @lyricalstring · oss under konar technologies</span>
      <span>alex@konar.es</span>
    </footer>

  </div>

</Base>


<style>
  @import "../../styles/case-study.css";

  /* ── OWNERSHIP TABLE: satstream has 4 columns (2fr 2fr 1fr 1fr) ── */
  .ownership-header,
  .ownership-row {
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 2fr 1fr 1fr;
  }
</style>
